    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0641" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v23/pg614"/>

                <head>280. Memorandum From Secretary of State Rusk to President Kennedy<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d280-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-07-26">July 26,
                    1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Talking Paper for your Meeting with Indonesian Foreign Minister
                        Subandrio</item>
                </list>
                <p>There is attached a talking paper for your meeting with Subandrio<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d280-f2"/> which includes a brief statement of the present status of
                    negotiations <pb facs="0642" n="615" xml:id="pg615"/> between the Dutch and
                    Indonesian representatives on the West New Guinea dispute. I am convinced of the
                    importance of your receiving Subandrio to express strongly the need for the
                    Indonesians to adopt the degree of flexibility necessary for achieving a
                    negotiated solution to this dispute and also to make clear to Subandrio that the
                    United States cannot be indifferent to the outbreak of major hostilities in the
                    area.</p>
                <p>It is intended that Ambassador Bunker will supplement this paper by an oral
                    briefing prior to your session with the Indonesian Foreign Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dean Rusk</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d280-a1.xml" xpointer="d280-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
